The builtin fixed-width types Word8.T .. Word64.T (this fork; see
LLVM-IR-backend-docs/fixed-width-integer-types-plan.md, Phase 4):
WordN.Wrap of INTEGERs and LONGINTs, including negative ones and
FIRST and LAST, keeps the low N bits, and widening the result again
gives x MOD 2^N; and at LAST (WordN.T), x + 1 > x is FALSE, both for
variables and for constants the front end folds.  Every line of output
should be the same with every backend and at every optimization level.
